        "behavior": "; 74125 — quad non-inverting 3-state buffer with four independent,\n; individually active-low output enables. Derived from the function table\n; (datasheet Table 3): with /nOE LOW the output nY follows data input nA;\n; with /nOE HIGH the output is in the high-impedance OFF-state.\n;\n; The four buffers are independent (each has its own enable), so each gets\n; its own 3-state pair. Bidirectional/3-state pins use GALasm's tristate\n; construct (galasmManual.txt section 3.4, established on the 74245): a .T\n; output equation fed from the data input, plus a single-term .E enable.\n;\n; Equations are physical-level GALasm: '/' is the complement operator and\n; signal names are this file's pin names with any active-low '/' prefix\n; dropped (pin /1OE is GAL signal 1OE, so '/1OE' below means \"pin /1OE is\n; LOW\"). The pin drives only while its .E term is true; when /nOE is HIGH\n; the .E term is false and nY is high-impedance.\n1Y.T = 1A\n1Y.E = /1OE\n2Y.T = 2A\n2Y.E = /2OE\n3Y.T = 3A\n3Y.E = /3OE\n4Y.T = 4A\n4Y.E = /4OE\n",
        "description": "Quad buffer/line driver, 3-state, individual active-low enables",
        "datasheet": {
          "vendor": "Nexperia",
          "title": "74HC125; 74HCT125 Quad buffer/line driver; 3-state",
          "rev": "Rev. 8, 22 February 2024",
          "url": "https://assets.nexperia.com/documents/data-sheet/74HC_HCT125.pdf"
        },
